# Environment variables this project's scripts read.
#
# Every one of these is optional: each script has a default, or does without.
# Copy to .env and fill in only what your machine needs — no script reads .env
# itself, so `set -a; . ./.env; set +a` or a plain export is what loads it.
#
# There are no secrets here. The Sparkle private key and the notarization
# credentials are deliberately not in the repository and not in this file.

# The Sparkle *bin directory* — the one holding generate_appcast, not the
# executable itself. Overrides tool discovery. Unset, scripts/verify-appcast.sh
# uses only the tools this checkout built into
# DerivedData/SourcePackages/artifacts/sparkle/Sparkle/bin and checks they belong
# to the pinned Sparkle version. The script appends /generate_appcast itself.
# SPARKLE_BIN=

# Set to 1 to skip the check that SPARKLE_BIN's tools sit beside a Sparkle source
# checkout tagged with the pinned version. For a CI image whose tools are
# installed elsewhere; never on the release machine. Unset means the check runs.
# SPARKLE_BIN_UNPINNED=

# Where fetched calendar provenance tables are cached between runs, for
# scripts/verify-data-sources.py. Defaults to
# ~/.cache/nepalkit-data-sources, and it caches either way: --offline reads
# whatever is in this directory. Override it for a test or a read-only
# environment, not to switch caching off.
# NEPAKIT_DATA_CACHE=

# Path to a local clone of the Homebrew tap, for scripts/update-cask.sh. It
# rewrites Casks/nepalkit.rb in that clone. Defaults to ../homebrew-tap beside
# this repository.
# NEPAKIT_TAP_DIR=

# Path to a built NepalKit.app's Info.plist, so scripts/run-app-tests.sh runs the
# five tests that read the shipped product instead of skipping them with a
# reason. Left unset the script discovers a product itself, but only uses one
# that is newer than the sources that build it. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
# NEPAKIT_BUILT_PLIST=
